ock\"><span class=\"kw2617\">std::<span class=\"me2\">chrono</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">file_time</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"coMULTI\">/*see below*/</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><br>&nbsp; &nbsp; from_sys<span class=\"br0\">(</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/chrono/system_clock\"><span class=\"kw2639\">std::<span class=\"me2\">chrono</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">sys_time</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>Duration<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> t <span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (2) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx20\">(since C++20)</span> <br><span class=\"t-mark\">(<span>optional*</span>)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">1)</span> Converts the <code>file_time</code> <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">t</span></code> to a <code>sys_time</code> representing the same point in time.</div>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">2)</span> Converts the <code>sys_time</code> <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">t</span></code> to a <code>file_time</code> representing the same point in time.</div>\n<p>The duration of the return type is computed from <code>Duration</code> in an unspecified manner.\n</p><p>These function templates are optional: an implementation may choose to instead provide <a href=\"/w/cpp/chrono/file_clock/to_from_utc\"><code>to_utc()</code></a> and <a href=\"/w/cpp/chrono/file_clock/to_from_utc\"><code>from_utc()</code></a>.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">1)</span> A <code>sys_time</code> representing the same point in time as the argument.</div>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">2)</span> A <code>file_time</code> representing the same point in time as the argument.</div>\n<h3 id=\"Notes\">Notes</h3>\n<p>User code should usually use <span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/chrono/clock_cast\"><span class=\"kw2562\">std::<span class=\"me2\">chrono</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">clock_cast</span></span></a></span>, which provides a generic interface to convert time points between clocks, rather than call these functions directly.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-notice\">This section is incomplete<br>Reason: no example </div>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/chrono/file_clock/to_from_utc\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>to_utc</span><span>from_utc</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-cmark\">[static]</span> <span class=\"t-mark\">(optional)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  converts between <code>file_time</code> and <code>utc_time</code> <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public static member function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/chrono/clock_cast\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>clock_cast</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx20\">(C++20)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  convert time points of one clock to another <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function template)</span> </td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":3,"text":"Notes","id":"Notes"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"chrono","title":"Date and time utilities"},{"path":"chrono/file_clock","title":"std::chrono::file_clock"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::chrono::file_clock::to_sys